(15) The control station shall be mounted or installed on the side of the limited-use/limited-application elevator within the reach of an individual in a wheelchair. The controls shall be mounted at a height between 36 inches and 48 inches above the finished floor;

(16) Hall controls shall be mounted on the latch side of the door and shall be located between 36 inches and 48 inches above the finished floor;

(17) The control on the limited-use/limited-application elevator shall include:

a. An emergency signaling device which conforms to the requirements of Section 8-9-192 of this Code and be operable at all times; and

b. An emergency stop switch as required by Section 8-9-158(6) of this Code;

(18) A separate fused disconnecting means, or circuit breaker, shall be provided on a separate electrical circuit in a machine room that is not accessible to the general public;

(19) Where required, a slack cable switch shall comply with requirements of Section 2.26.2.1 of the ASME Code;

(20) The installation of pipes or ducts conveying gases, vapors, or liquids in hoistways, machine rooms, or machinery spaces shall comply with the requirements of Section 2.8.2 of the ASME Code. Only electrical wiring used directly in connection with a limited-use/limited-application elevator may be installed inside the hoistway, machinery space, machine room, or control room and shall comply with the requirements of Section 2.8.1.1 of the ASME Code. Electrical wiring and components in a limited-use/limited-application elevator and their installation shall comply with the requirements of Chapter 8, Article III, of the 2019 Detroit City Code, *Electrical Code*;

(21) The hoistway for the elevator shall be fully enclosed. The hoistway enclosure and the entrance assemblies shall have a fire resistance rating of not less than one hour. The enclosure shall not deflect more than one inch when subjected to a force of 100 pounds applied horizontally at any point. In addition, where an elevator is exposed to the outside elements, a permanent weatherproof enclosure, which shall be made of approved construction materials, shall be provided for the device.

(22) The hoistway entrances of a limited-use/limited-application elevator shall be guarded by doors of unperforated construction. The doors shall be of the delayed self-closing type that are not less than 80 inches in height, and provide a minimum clear opening width of 30 inches when the doors are on the short side of the platform or a minimum clear opening width of 40 inches when the doors are on the long side of the platform. The doors shall have an approved combination mechanical lock and electrical contacts, and shall open only when the car platform is within one-half inch of the floor level;

(23) The running clearance between the edge of the platform sill and the landing sill shall not be less than three-eighths of an inch or more than three-fourths of an inch. The distance between the edge of the hoistway landing sill to the hoistway face of the door shall not be more than three inches. The distance between the hoistway face of the landing door and the limited-use/limited-application device door shall not be more than five inches;

(24) A minimum 30 second non-interference feature shall be provided and shall assure that the first call registered will control the operation of the elevator;

(25) The limited-use/limited-application elevator platform floor surfacing shall be of a slip-resistant type;

(26) Where a platform of a limited-use/limited-application elevator does not have an under-platform clearance of 48 inches, or the maximum rise to the elevator, whichever is less, when resting on its bottom mechanical limits, the elevator shall incorporate a means which, when appropriately positioned during maintenance, will mechanically prevent the platform from descending closer than 48 inches to the pit floor at rated speed with rated load in the down direction. Instructions shall be posted in the pit;

(27) Platform guide rails shall be of metal construction. Steel construction shall conform to the

