requirements of Section 2.23.2.1 of the ASME Code, and metals other than steel shall conform to Section 2.23.2.2 of the ASME Code. The top and bottom ends of each run of guide rail shall be so located in relation to the extreme positions of travel of the barrier-free device that the device guiding members cannot travel beyond the ends of the guide rails. Fastenings, deflection, and joints shall conform to the requirements set forth in Sections 2.23.2, 2.23.5, and 2.23.8 of the ASME Code;

(28) Machines, machinery, and sheaves shall be supported and maintained in place to prevent any part from becoming loose of displaced under the conditions imposed in service and shall comply with the requirements of Section 2.9 of the ASME Code;

(29) A stop switch shall be provided on the top of a limited-use/limited-application device;

(30) A production model of a limited-use/limited-application elevator shall be subjected to a static load test to establish that all structural components of the elevator will withstand stresses of ten times the rated load of the elevator and to ensure a factor of safety of not less than ten. A registered professional engineer shall certify the safety factor, and affix his or her signature and seal to the certification;

(31) A limited-use/limited-application elevator shall not be used for moving freight; and

(32) A limited-use/limited-application elevator shall be serviced and examined for defects at least once every 90 days by an unlimited-elevator journeyperson who is licensed by the City.

(b) The following components of limited-use/limited-application elevators shall conform to, and be tested in accordance with, the indicated requirements:

(1) The driving machine shall be of the traction or direct-plunger hydraulic type. Traction machines shall conform to the requirements of Section 2.24 of the ASME Code;

(2) Terminal stopping devices shall be provided for traction driving machines and shall conform to the requirements of Section 2.25 of the ASME Code;

(3) Tests for traction driving machines shall be conducted in accordance with the requirements of Sections 8.10, 8.11.2.2, and 8.11.1.3 of the ASME Code;

(4) Direct-plunger hydraulic driving machines shall conform to the requirements of Sections 3.18.1.1 and 3.19.1 of the ASME Code;

(5) Terminal stopping devices and control circuits shall be provided for direct-plunger machines and shall conform to the requirements of Sections 3.25.1 and 3.26.6 of the ASME Code; and

(6) Tests for direct-plunger hydraulic machines shall be conducted in accordance with the requirements of Section 8-9-178 of this Code.

