(b) Subject summaries. The utility shall consult with the city council and the collaborative working group to determine subject areas of the plan likely to be of interest to the public. The utility shall prepare a summary of its plan pertaining to each such subject area. Each subject summary shall include the utility’s proposed activities, findings and analyses pertaining to the subject area, together with underlying technical information to support them. The subject summary shall contain information more detailed than the executive summary, but less detailed than the technical volumes.

(c) Three-year action plan. Each plan shall include a three-year action plan which describes the proposed resource acquisition actions which the utility shall take prior to the approval of the next plan, and contains the information required in sections 158-783 through 158-787.

(d) Technical volume. Each plan shall include technical volumes which shall contain the information required by sections 158-769 through 158-782.

(e) Technical appendix. Each plan shall include a technical appendix. The appendix may be contained within the technical volume, but shall contain the following:

(1) Sufficient detail to enable the technically proficient reader to understand how the plan and its forecasts were prepared and to verify the reasonableness of the assumptions, and the data and the methods used in developing the plan.

(2) All significant information used in the plan.

(3) Documentation, inputs, and summary outputs for all models and formulas used.

(f) Standard documents. As part of its plan filing, each utility shall include for itself and for the system:

(1) Its annual report to stockholders for the most recent two years;

(2) Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC) Form 1 for the most recent two years;

(3) Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) Form 8K and 10K for the most recent two years;

(4) Energy Information Administration (EIA) Form 767 for the most recent two years.

(g) Financial information. The following financial assumptions and models used in the plan shall be fully described:

(1) Those assumptions which shall be stated and justified include at a minimum:

a. The general rate of inflation;

b. The AFUDC rates used in the plan;

c. The cost-of-capital rates used in the plan;

d. The discount rate used in the calculations to determine present worth;

e. The tax rates used in the plan.

(2) The plan shall include at a minimum the following financial information, together with supporting documentation and justification:

a. Present worth of revenue requirements for the preferred and each alternative resource plan considered for evaluation and risk analysis, using the discount rate;

b. Nominal revenue requirements by year;

